the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:

*a benefit* for *a criminal* for *a crime* is in order.
*a person* was provoked by *an other person* to commit *a crime*.
*a criminal* felt provoked into *a crime* by *an action* of *a person*. 
*a person* did perform *an act* towards *a second person* that induces *a crime*. 

the knowledge base includes:

leniency for a criminal for a crime is in order if
	the criminal was provoked by an other person to commit the crime.
	
a criminal was provoked by a person to commit a crime if
	the criminal felt provoked into the crime by an action of the person
	and the person did perform the action towards the criminal that induces the crime. 

scenario standard is:
    the criminal felt provoked into raping by some non-aggressive attitude of the victim.
    the criminal felt provoked into killing by some non-aggressive attitude of the victim.
    	
scenario misogynistic is:
    the criminal felt provoked into raping by some non-aggressive attitude of the victim.
    the criminal felt provoked into killing by some non-aggressive attitude of the victim.
    the victim did perform some non-aggressive attitude towards the criminal that induces raping.

query one is:
    which person was provoked by which person to commit which crime.
